Amy: Really? Where is it?
Shen Qi: At the Wuhan Stadium, on Saturday afternoon.
Amy: That sounds fun. Who is playing?
Shen Qi: Wuhan against Guangzhou. Would you like to come along?
Amy: I''d love to! What time does it start?
Shen Qi: At three o''clock. Let''s meet at the gate at two thirty.
Amy: Great. See you then!', '申奇问 Amy 周末有场足球赛;在武汉体育场,周六下午;武汉对广州;申奇邀她一起去;Amy 很乐意;比赛三点开始;两点半在门口见。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What event is Shen Qi inviting Amy to?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["A soccer game.","A boxing match.","A ski race.","A marathon."]},{"q":"Where will the game take place?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["At the gym.","At the Wuhan Stadium.","At the school track.","In a park."]},{"q":"Which two teams are playing?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Wuhan and Guangzhou.","Beijing and Shanghai.","Wuhan and Beijing.","Two school teams."]},{"q":"What time does the game start?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["At two o''clock.","At three o''clock.","At two thirty.","At four o''clock."]},{"q":"Where will they meet?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["At Amy''s home.","On the bus.","At the stadium gate.","At the train station."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required1', 'U3');
As a player, she brought honour and glory to her country.
As a coach, she led the team to medals at the Olympics.
When two key players were lost before a big match, she did not lose heart.
She believed her young players could win if they worked as a team.', '郎平深受国内外排球迷喜爱;作为球员,她为祖国带来荣誉;作为教练,她带队在奥运会上夺牌;大赛前失去两名主力,她没有泄气;她相信只要团结,年轻队员就能赢。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Who loves Lang Ping, according to the passage?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Only her family.","Only her students.","Nobody.","Volleyball fans at home and abroad."]},{"q":"What did she do as a player?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["She brought honour to her country.","She gave up early.","She refused to train.","She lost every game."]},{"q":"What did she lead her team to as a coach?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Nothing at all.","Medals at the Olympics.","A single practice.","A holiday abroad."]},{"q":"How did she react when two key players were lost?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["She quit at once.","She blamed the team.","She did not lose heart.","She cancelled the match."]},{"q":"What did Lang Ping believe about her young players?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["They would surely fail.","They were too weak.","They should leave.","They could win by working as a team."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required1', 'U3');
Dave: Yes, it''s great. Is this your first time here?
Jack: Actually, it is. You come here often, don''t you?
Dave: Yes, at least three times a week.
Jack: You''ve lost some weight, haven''t you?
Dave: I have. All that fat has become muscle now.
Jack: It won''t make me too tired, will it?
Dave: Maybe at first, but you''ll get used to it.', 'Jack 觉得健身房很棒;这是他第一次来;Dave 常来,每周至少三次;Jack 说 Dave 瘦了;Dave 说脂肪变成了肌肉;Jack 担心太累;Dave 说开始会,但会习惯。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Is this Jack''s first time at the gym?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Yes, it is.","No, he comes daily.","No, he came last year.","He never goes."]},{"q":"How often does Dave go to the gym?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Once a month.","At least three times a week.","Every day.","Never."]},{"q":"What has happened to Dave''s body?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["He has gained weight.","Nothing has changed.","His fat has become muscle.","He has got weaker."]},{"q":"What is Jack worried about?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["The price.","The time.","The coach.","Getting too tired."]},{"q":"What does Dave say about feeling tired?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["He will get used to it.","It will last forever.","It means he should stop.","It is dangerous."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required1', 'U3');
Every morning I run slowly around the park for half an hour.
Jogging is good for my body and helps me deal with stress.
After a hard day at school, a short run always clears my mind.
I don''t run to win a medal; I run to feel happy and fit.', '我最喜欢的健康方式是慢跑;每天早晨绕公园慢跑半小时;慢跑有益身体,还能缓解压力;辛苦一天后,短跑总能让头脑清醒;我跑步不是为了奖牌,而是为了快乐和健康。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What is the speaker''s favourite way to stay healthy?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Boxing.","Jogging.","Skiing.","Swimming."]},{"q":"When does the speaker jog?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Late at night.","Only on weekends.","Every morning.","Once a month."]},{"q":"Besides the body, what else does jogging help with?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Making money.","Learning English.","Cooking meals.","Dealing with stress."]},{"q":"What does a short run do after a hard day?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["It clears the speaker''s mind.","It makes the speaker angry.","It wastes time.","It causes injuries."]},{"q":"Why does the speaker run?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["To win medals.","To feel happy and fit.","To beat others.","To become famous."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required1', 'U3');
Lily: Exactly. Cheating is always wrong.
Cao Jing: But an athlete should also do his best to win for the fans.
Max: Doing your best is fine, but you must play fair.
Lily: Right. The audience wants honest games.
Cao Jing: I see what you mean. A win by cheating is not a real win.
Max: That''s true. Good sportsmanship matters more than the score.
Lily: I agree with that completely.', 'Max 说球员不该假摔,哪怕为了帮队;Lily 赞同,作弊总是错的;曹静说运动员也该为球迷尽力争胜;Max 说尽力可以但要公平;Lily 说观众想看诚实的比赛;曹静认同,靠作弊赢不算真赢;Max 说体育精神比比分更重要;Lily 完全同意。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What does Max think a player should never do?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Train hard.","Help teammates.","Pretend to fall down.","Win a game."]},{"q":"What is Lily''s opinion about cheating?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["It is clever.","It is necessary.","It is fun.","It is always wrong."]},{"q":"What does Cao Jing first say an athlete should do?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Do his best to win for the fans.","Give up early.","Cheat to win.","Leave the team."]},{"q":"What does the audience want, according to Lily?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["A long game.","Honest games.","A free ticket.","More noise."]},{"q":"What do they finally agree on?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Winning is everything.","Cheating helps the team.","Good sportsmanship matters more than the score.","The score is all that counts."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required1', 'U3');
Don''t try to do too much exercise all at once.
It is better to train a little every day rather than for hours once a week.
Choose a sport you enjoy, like jogging, badminton, or swimming.
When exercise is fun, you will keep doing it and stay healthy.', '给想保持健康的人一个小贴士:别一次做太多运动;每天练一点,比一周一次练几个小时更好;选一项你喜欢的运动,比如慢跑、羽毛球或游泳;当运动有趣时,你就会坚持下去,保持健康。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Who is this tip for?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Only athletes.","Only coaches.","Only children.","Anyone who wants to stay fit."]},{"q":"What does the speaker warn against?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Doing too much exercise all at once.","Eating fruit.","Sleeping early.","Drinking water."]},{"q":"What is better than training for hours once a week?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Never training.","Training a little every day.","Only watching sports.","Training all night."]},{"q":"What kind of sport should you choose?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["The hardest one.","The most expensive one.","One that you enjoy.","One nobody likes."]},{"q":"What happens when exercise is fun?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["You stop quickly.","You get bored.","You feel worse.","You keep doing it and stay healthy."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required1', 'U3');

